@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: siege lines are a placed, legal structure the tutorial must have the player draw — not a painted overlay
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no siege-line type exists under the sandbox
'   checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning engine and tutorial
'   modules before a covers: line can be honest.
'   the runner that sequences this beat _spec/_plans/tutorial-interactive-siege.puml
'   ships that may need a line ......... _spec/_plans/tutorial-ships.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "siege lines" is a PIECE OF SIEGE, not the whole mode. The player has to
' understand what a line is, where it may be placed, and what it forbids. The
' beat is placement (or breaking) of a real line.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   supply, fire, movement block, or scoring
'   how many segments, and who may cut them
'   whether lines are units, terrain, or a overlay with hit rules
'
' Painting a dashed overlay the engine does not know will desync the
' interactive siege: the player "places a line" and the live game has none.
title PLANNED — the player places a real siege line;\na painted overlay is not a line

component "siege line (engine)" as LINE <<app>>
component "legal place / cut" as ACT <<app>>
component "tutorial beat" as BEAT <<app>>
component "**painted overlay**\nengine has no line" as PAINT <<error>>
component "interactive siege runner" as RUN <<app>>
component "ships that need a line" as SHIP <<app>>

BEAT ARROW_MAIN ACT
ACT ARROW_MAIN LINE
BEAT ARROW_ERROR PAINT
RUN ARROW_MAIN BEAT
SHIP ARROW_OPTIONAL LINE

note bottom of PAINT
  **Without an engine query it is not a siege
  line, however convincing the overlay
  illustration.** The beat finishes only when a
  line object exists on the square the player
  selected.
end note

note bottom of ACT
  **Placement and severance are separate verbs and
  must not share a single tutorial beat.** Mixing
  them conceals which placement rule failed when
  the player is marked incorrect.
end note

note right of LINE
  **A siege line is the atomic object the
  interactive runner sequences, together with
  ships.** Without a real line type that mode has
  nothing legal to gate.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Find the line type.** What stores a siege line, what makes placement
  illegal, what a unit does when it meets one. No tutorial copy until those
  symbols exist.
  --
  **2. One placement beat.** Player draws a legal line; engine accepts;
  illegal tiles stay dead. Then, if needed, a second beat that cuts.
  ==
  **3. Hand the object to the runner.** tutorial-interactive-siege.puml
  sequences this beat; it does not duplicate the placement rule.
  --
  **Left open**: geometry (straight, hex, orthogonal); who pays to place;
  whether a line is visible through fog.
end legend
@enduml
